# Normalise line endings in the repository, and check out LF everywhere.
#
# Why this file exists: without it, Git on Windows checks files out as CRLF and
# stores them as LF, so the same file has different bytes depending on who
# committed it. That produces whole-file diffs, makes `git blame` attribute
# unrelated lines, and means CI on Linux and a contributor on Windows are not
# looking at the same source. The warnings during `git add` ("LF will be replaced
# by CRLF") were the symptom.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` makes the repository authoritative: LF in the object store,
# LF in every working copy. Node, TypeScript and the test suite all handle LF
# natively on Windows, so nothing needs CRLF here.
* text=auto eol=lf

# These are executed by Windows, where a shebang line ending in CR is a real
# problem, and by nothing else. Explicit rather than left to the global rule.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Lockfiles and generated bundles are not hand-edited; keep diffs honest.
package-lock.json -diff
*.vsix binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
